<<~ ahu slot=`#/bearing`>>
! Reception QA

Compare an observed artifact with a known Art Sigil and any optional [[Artifact Contract|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/artifact-contract]]. Use [[Formal Analysis|ha.ka.ba/lares/api/art-sigils/formal-analysis]] for open-ended reading of an existing image. Neither process recovers a hidden original prompt.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/checks`>>
!! Three independent judgments

* `Technical` — required dimensions, alpha, cropping, registration, file integrity, exact text and editability.
* `Artistic` — worktype, primary read, hierarchy, material behavior, relation, depiction-scope and deliberate silence.
* `Situated` — legibility at intended size, context, audience distance, display or composite.

Mark each `fulfilled`, `deviated`, `failed` or `unverified`. Attach an observation, not just a grade. Avoid combining the three into a single success scalar.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/loop`>>
!! Observe → compare → intervene → inspect → hold

1. Retain the current artifact, source, references and known receiver conditions.
2. Record visible differences and affected regions. Do not guess unseen model operations.
3. Check artistic requirements separately from mandatory artifact requirements.
4. Choose the smallest appropriate correction or retain a valuable departure by explicit operator choice.
5. Inspect the result and before/after comparison under the same conditions.
6. Keep rollback; record acceptance and remaining uncertainties. Stop when the operator's criteria are met.

Changing several variables at once prevents claims about which one caused an improvement. Selecting a favorite from a small set does not establish population-level performance.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/cases`>>
!! Probe cases

| Work | Verify | Do not mistake |
|---|---|---|
| Transparent overlay | Actual alpha and composite role | Transparent appearance for zero-alpha margins |
| Sparse abstract field | Intentional silence and nonrepresentation | More detail for better fulfillment |
| Single photograph | Framing and documented source status | Attractive narrative for documentary evidence |
| Mixed-media work | Distinct material responses | One uniform simulated texture for separate supports |
| Typography | Exact characters and intended hierarchy | Plausible-looking text for exact spelling |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/record`>>
!! Review record

```toml
[review]
art_sigil = "replace with originating Inscription or Folio"
artifact_contract = "reference or absent"
technical = "status, evidence"
artistic = "status, evidence"
situated = "status, evidence"
decision = "operator acceptance, rejection or hold"
rollback = "retained source"
```

<<~/ahu>>

